# Team Template: ERP Implementation — Overview

## Team Composition (10 FTE, 36 weeks)

| Role | Count | Allocation | Rate | Weekly Cost |
|------|-------|------------|------|-------------|
| Program Director | 1 | 50% | $2,000 | $5,000 |
| Engagement Manager | 1 | 100% | $1,800 | $9,000 |
| Solution Architect | 1 | 100% | $1,600 | $8,000 |
| Oracle Cloud Specialist | 2 | 100% | $1,500 | $15,000 |
| Sr. Consultant — Finance | 1 | 100% | $1,400 | $7,000 |
| Consultant — Technical | 2 | 100% | $1,100 | $11,000 |
| Change Management Lead | 1 | 50% | $1,300 | $3,250 |
| QA Engineer | 1 | 100% | $900 | $4,500 |

**Total weekly onshore cost**: ~$62,750
**36-week engagement**: ~$720,000 (professional services)

## Key Responsibilities
- **Program Director**: Multi-workstream governance, vendor management, C-suite relationship
- **Engagement Manager**: Day-to-day PM, sprint planning, resource coordination, dashboards
- **Solution Architect**: ERP configuration, integration design, customization decisions
- **Oracle Specialists**: GL/AP/AR/Cash Management module configuration, security roles
- **Senior Consultant**: Business process reengineering, chart of accounts, close optimization
- **Technical Consultants**: Custom reports, workflows, data migration scripts, integrations
- **Change Management Lead**: Stakeholder analysis, communication, training, adoption metrics
- **QA Engineer**: Test strategy, automated scripts, regression testing, defect tracking

## Governance Cadence
- Daily sync (15 min, core team)
- Workstream leads sync (3x/week, 30 min)
- Bi-weekly sprint review (2 hours, with client SMEs)
- Monthly program steering (2 hours, C-suite)

## Scaling Options
- **Small** (<$400K): Reduce to 6 FTE, 24 weeks, focus on single module
- **Large** (>$1M): Add second Solution Architect, offshore development team
- **Global** (>$2M): Multi-phase rollout with regional deployment teams
